{
  "_status": "PROPOSAL (Kimi B, 2026-11-17). Awaits Claude freeze with the other M2.5 contracts. All faiths/cultures/jurisdictions are FICTIONAL game presets; nothing here asserts anything about real laws, faiths or people. Orientation/belief/culture defaults are never inferred from names, gender or complexion.",
  "catalog_version": "policy-1.0.0",
  "description": "Save-local, versioned policy catalogs: fictional faith profiles (public tenets), cultures, jurisdiction law presets, and the personal attraction/preference profile schema. Presets are a per-save BASELINE: the editor or content may create save-local overrides without mutating the catalog; a later catalog/content update must not silently erase save-local edits (baseline+override+version, spec 02-contracts.md §3).",
  "save_local_semantics": {
    "resolution_order": "save_local_override (if present) -> catalog preset (by id+version) -> built-in neutral default",
    "content_update_rule": "updating catalog data bumps catalog_version; existing saves keep their resolved profiles unless the player opts in; no silent erase",
    "neutral_default": "any unknown/missing id resolves to the neutral default in `defaults.neutral_profile`; unknown/missing tenet stance resolves to `neutral`"
  },
  "union_recognition_shape": {
    "_owner": "A owns the union edge; A accepted this sub-shape and B ADOPTS A's exact values (graph-contract.md §3.2)",
    "status": "recognized | civil_only | unrecognized | forbidden",
    "jurisdiction_id": "string, references jurisdiction_presets[].id or a save-local override id",
    "law_version": "int, per-jurisdiction save-local revision in force when the union was formed or last reprojected (bumps on editor jurisdiction edits; separate from the catalog semver)",
    "basis": "ceremony | registration | common_law",
    "_notes": "Recognition is projected state, not a ban: a forbidden/unrecognized union still exists as an edge and carries social/legal consequences. Editor law edits reproject CURRENT recognition only; they never rewrite historical law_version on old unions."
  },
